---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHero from '../../components/PageHero.astro';
import { business, instagramDm, companyDisclosure, hasCompany } from '../../data/business';

/* Change this date whenever the policy changes */
const updated = '12 October 2026';
---
<Base page="privacy">
  <PageHero page="privacy" kicker="Your data"
    lede="What personal information this website collects, why we collect it, who sees it and what your rights are." />
  <div class="paper">
    <div class="paper-in prose">
      <p><strong>Last updated: {updated}</strong></p>

      <h2>Who we are</h2>
      <p>{business.name} is responsible for (the “controller” of) the personal information collected through this website.{companyDisclosure && <> {companyDisclosure}</>}</p>
      <p>To ask about this policy or your information, {business.email && <>email <a href={`mailto:${business.email}`}>{business.email}</a>, </>}message us on Instagram at <a href={instagramDm}>@{business.instagram}</a>{hasCompany && <> or write to us at our registered office: {business.company.registeredOffice}</>}.</p>

      <h2>What we collect and why</h2>
      <h3>When you send an enquiry</h3>
      <p>Our <a href="/enquire/">enquiry form</a> asks for your name, a phone number or email address, what the enquiry is for, an optional date and number of guests, and your message. We use these details only to reply to you and to arrange anything you ask us for.</p>
      <p>Our lawful basis is taking steps you ask for before an order (for parties, events and big orders) and our legitimate interest in answering the questions people send us.</p>

      <h3>When you message us on Instagram</h3>
      <p>If you contact us through Instagram, Meta handles your messages under its own privacy policy. We use what you send us only to reply.</p>

      <h3>When you visit this website</h3>
      <p>We use Cloudflare Web Analytics to count visits and see which pages are useful. It does not use cookies or similar technology, does not follow you across other websites and does not build a profile of you. It gives us totals, such as page views, the website that sent you here, your country and the type of device you used. Our lawful basis is our legitimate interest in understanding how the website is used so we can improve it.</p>
      <p>The company that hosts this website, Netlify, keeps short-term technical logs, including IP addresses, to keep the website secure and running.</p>

      <h2>Cookies</h2>
      <p>This website does not set any cookies. Because our visitor statistics do not use cookies, we do not need to ask for your consent and you will not see a cookie banner. If we ever add anything that uses cookies or similar technology and is not strictly necessary, we will ask for your consent first and update this page.</p>

      <h2>Who we share it with</h2>
      <p>We do not sell your information or share it for marketing. These companies process information for us, under contract and only on our instructions:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Netlify, Inc.</strong> hosts this website and stores enquiry form messages.</li>
        <li><strong>Cloudflare, Inc.</strong> provides our cookie-free visitor statistics.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Both are based in the United States. When information is transferred outside the UK, it is protected by the safeguards UK law requires, such as the UK–US data bridge or the UK International Data Transfer Addendum.</p>
      <p>We may also share information if the law requires us to.</p>

      <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Enquiries:</strong> up to 12 months after we last hear from you, then deleted, unless the enquiry becomes an order we must keep records of.</li>
        <li><strong>Hosting logs:</strong> kept by Netlify for a short period, then deleted.</li>
        <li><strong>Visitor statistics:</strong> totals only, with nothing that identifies you.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>Under UK data protection law you can ask us to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>give you a copy of the information we hold about you;</li>
        <li>correct anything that is wrong;</li>
        <li>delete your information;</li>
        <li>limit how we use it, or stop using it where we rely on legitimate interests;</li>
        <li>send it to you or another organisation in a common format.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>To use any of these rights, contact us using the details under “Who we are”. It’s free, and we will reply within one month.</p>

      <h2>Complaints</h2>
      <p>If you’re unhappy with how we’ve handled your information, please tell us first so we can put it right. You can also complain to the Information Commissioner’s Office (ICO) at <a href="https://ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint/">ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint</a> or on 0303 123 1113.</p>

      <h2>Other websites</h2>
      <p>This website links to Instagram, Google Maps and Apple Maps. They have their own privacy policies, and we are not responsible for how they use your information.</p>

      <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>We will update this page if anything changes. The date at the top shows when it last changed.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
